.TH tupngpad n 0.3 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tupngpad
.PP
Normalise a set of (transparent) PNGs to a uniform size. Typical use: object cut\-outs saved as transparent PNGs, each cropped to its own tight bounding box. \fBtupngpad\fR brings them all to one common size, centres each one, keeps a margin around the content, and flattens transparency onto a background colour (e.g. white). Pure Tcl, no Tk and no external packages; the pixel work pairs with \fBtclutils::tupng\fR / \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR.
.SS API
.CS
package require tclutils::tupngpad

# normalise every PNG in $files into /out, all the same size
tclutils::tupngpad::batch $files /out -margin 4 -background white
.CE
.SS File\-level
.PP
\fBtupngpad::batch files outdir ?options?\fR — read each PNG in \fBfiles\fR, optionally trim it to its content, then pad every image to one common size and write the result into \fBoutdir\fR (same base name). Returns a dict \fB{size {tw th} files {in1 out1 in2 out2 ...}}\fR: the common output size and the input/output paths in pairs. All options are checked before any file is read. A failed write leaves an existing output file (0.3, \fBcommon::replaceFile\fR).
.PP
Options:
.IP \(bu
\fB\-margin N\fR — empty space kept around the content, in pixels (default \fB4\fR).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-background COLOR\fR — colour the formerly transparent area is flattened onto (default \fBwhite\fR; same colour forms as \fBtupngdraw\fR).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-trim BOOL\fR — crop each input to its content bounding box first (default \fB1\fR).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-align A\fR — placement of the content in the padded canvas: \fBcenter\fR (default), \fBnw\fR, \fBn\fR, \fBne\fR, \fBw\fR, \fBe\fR, \fBsw\fR, \fBs\fR, \fBse\fR. Any other value is an error (\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON VALUE \-align}\fR, the message lists the allowed ones).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-square BOOL\fR — force a square output (default \fB0\fR).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-size {W H}\fR — force the inner content area (positive integers); default is the maximum content size found across all inputs.
.SS "Pixel\-level primitives"
.PP
These operate on an RGBA pixel buffer (\fBrgba\fR) of width \fBw\fR and height \fBh\fR, as produced/consumed by the \fBtupng\fR layer:
.IP \(bu
\fBtupngpad::bbox rgba w h\fR — return the content bounding box \fB{x0 y0 x1 y1}\fR (the non\-transparent extent).
.IP \(bu
\fBtupngpad::trim rgba w h\fR — crop the buffer to its bounding box.
.IP \(bu
\fBtupngpad::padTo rgba w h tw th ?options?\fR — centre/place the content inside a \fBtw\fR×\fBth\fR canvas and return PNG bytes. Options: \fB\-background COLOR\fR (default \fBwhite\fR), \fB\-align A\fR (as above), \fB\-filter {}\fR (empty = \fBup\fR).
.PP
Semi\-transparent pixels are composited source\-over onto the background (\fBtupngdraw paste\fR): on an opaque background they become opaque blends, on a transparent background (\fB\-background transparent\fR) they keep their colour and alpha.
.SS Errors
.TS
l l.
Error code	Cause
\fB{TCLUTILS TUPNGPAD MARGIN}\fR	\fB\-margin\fR not an integer >= 0
\fB{TCLUTILS TUPNGPAD TRIM}\fR	\fB\-trim\fR not a boolean
\fB{TCLUTILS TUPNGPAD SQUARE}\fR	\fB\-square\fR not a boolean
\fB{TCLUTILS TUPNGPAD SIZE}\fR	\fB\-size\fR not empty or \fB{W H}\fR with integers >= 1
\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON VALUE \-align}\fR	unknown \fB\-align\fR
.TE
.PP
Errors from reading and decoding the files (\fBopen\fR, \fBtupng::decode\fR) pass through unchanged.
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Pure Tcl, no Tk, no external dependencies (TclOO/\fBclock\fR/core only).
.IP \(bu
Designed to chain with \fBtupng\fR/\fBtupngdraw\fR: decode → \fBtrim\fR/\fBpadTo\fR → encode.
